{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner","id":1016039,"title":"Does the Nimbus affect the Owner?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-12T02:51:02-08:00","id":1016039,"title":"Does the Nimbus affect the Owner?","content":"Well.. I think the title pretty well explains my question..<br /> Played some 1st edition mage and the nimbus didn't have nearly as big an impact on the game as in 2nd editon. But I am a little uncertain if the nimbus tilt also affects the owner?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T05:35:06-08:00","id":1016076,"title":"","content":"Nobody knows. Nimbus tilt rules are terribly written. Great idea, horrible execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T05:53:19-08:00","id":1016078,"title":"","content":"I run with no, in part because it means you'll rarely have players picking negative effects for their nimbus and in part because I think it doesn't make sense that your own magical aura would reflect back on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T07:18:46-08:00","id":1016098,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> <br /> (characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T08:46:12-08:00","id":1016120,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they don't; Nimbus rules state they affect witnesses, which infers preclusion of the actor themselves.<br /> <br /> I recommend houseruling Nimbuses, though; they're pretty clunky RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T09:22:37-08:00","id":1016136,"title":"","content":"A mage's nimbus does not affect him, but will still affect friends and allies. Unlike the Vampire and Werewolf &quot;aura&quot; effects, a mage's nimbus is not targeted or particularly discrimination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T02:16:08-08:00","id":1016465,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarifications guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1016120#post1016120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, they don't; Nimbus rules state they affect witnesses, which infers preclusion of the actor themselves.<br /> <br /> I recommend houseruling Nimbuses, though; they're pretty clunky RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>After some looking at it, me and my players have also come to this conclusion. We love how the nimbus (and primal urge, the beast, ect..) have become more than just an fluff effect, and something the players could bring forth to showoff their characters supernatural prowess (REALLY love the vampire mechanics).<br /> <br /> But we said the same as you: it felt clunky and we also felt it was even more out of the players control compared to the other supernatural beings special nifty-power-trait-thing.<br /> <br /> - every time a spell was cast, the effects of the nimbus would trigger<br /> - if more than one mage was present, it would become a bonus/penalty-chaos<br /> - dependent on potency, it had a chance of affecting all allies with a negative effect (and a positive)<br /> - also dependent on potency, it could also grant enemies a bonus (and a penalty)<br /> <br /> We thought about adding a personal nimbus effect for casting spells and a flared effect. The first grants a bonus and the second a appropriate penalty based on the bonus.<br /> It still suffers from some of the points above though, and might also add to much extra power to the mage.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should make a different thread about house ruled nimbus effects..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T02:38:28-08:00","id":1016469,"title":"","content":"Remember that nimbus affects only mages that perceive it and it means that they need to have AMS on. When you fight you don't have it on unless you are trying to dispell enemy magic because it gives you a -2 penalty to everything you do that is not a mage sight or related to magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-13-2016, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T02:43:34-08:00","id":1016470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1016469#post1016469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that nimbus affects only mages that perceive it and it means that they need to have AMS on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bar a mage forcing a nimbus flare, or success in a contest of auras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T03:04:01-08:00","id":1016475,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a> Yea... Forced nimbus is incredibly weak. Having 3 Gnosis and adding WP you have 6 dice so roughly 2 successes on its potency that is withstood by resistance attribute. So if you if you are not facing children and weakest adults it won't work. Forget about mages or other splats. It works well as defence mechanism though, since it adds your resistance attribute.<br /> <br /> But actually I like the mechanics. Starting mage can do nothing but there are merits that can change that and all in all its pretty well balanced.<br /> <br /> Edit: As to the mayhem that can arise when you have 4 active nimbi with different durations I advice to craft conditions out of them beforehand and write down on cards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-13-2016, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T03:05:19-08:00","id":1016476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1016469#post1016469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that nimbus affects only mages that perceive it and it means that they need to have AMS on. When you fight you don't have it on unless you are trying to dispell enemy magic because it gives you a -2 penalty to everything you do that is not a mage sight or related to magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not according to the rules. So its still gona be a bonus/penalty hell with multiple mages.<br /> <br /> p. 89<br /> &quot;While characters without Mage Sight cannot see the aura, the subtle cues still affect them with the Tilt. This is almost always imperceptible, but some particularly clued-in witnesses may note when something\u2019s awry.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T03:36:06-08:00","id":1016479,"title":"","content":"Heh. What sorcery is this? You are right, but I'm right too.<br /> <br /> p89 - paragraph above yours.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deliberate flares like this are visible even in the Fallen<br /> World and can therefore affect characters not using Mage Sight,<br /> although Sleepers will suffer Quiescence after the Tilt ends. </div> </div> </div>It's contradictory... Well. I think that you are <i>rightier </i>but I don't see any of the mess with nimbi at my table using my wrong interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:06:29-08:00","id":1016552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1016465#post1016465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We thought about adding a personal nimbus effect for casting spells and a flared effect. The first grants a bonus and the second a appropriate penalty based on the bonus.<br /> It still suffers from some of the points above though, and might also add to much extra power to the mage.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should make a different thread about house ruled nimbus effects..</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is as good as anywhere.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972619-has-immediate-nimbus-come-up-in-your-games?p=981677#post981677\">These are my house rules.</a> They've come up often enough that they've been interesting.<br /> <br /> Everyone's game is different, so they might not work for you, but they might help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T03:37:37-08:00","id":1017571,"title":"","content":"Thats somewhat more like it. The dim effect seems a little off to me though. I am not if it is me or if I can put my finger on it:<br /> <br /> - The bonus applies against everybody (seems strong)<br /> - I don't think the drawback is that special. It does what every other spell does. I know there is the extra things you described, but I imagene these things happening due to the below reason<br /> - It kinda seems like something you would use on sleepers since they forget it, but that would be a breaking point for them (I seem to recall witnessing supernatural things is a breaking point, and if so, they would connect that breaking point to the mage).<br /> <br /> The Flash of Enlightenment also seems abit powerful with how long it can last. But that might just be me and I can get use to it.<br /> But in general, the mechanic works well for a flared nimbus effect. It can be powerful/useful when used right, and the players have control over when to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:25:34-08:00","id":1017586,"title":"","content":"A bare-bone snip of my homebrew:<ul><li><b>Fractal Nimbus</b>: The Long-Term Nimbus, but described more as a mystery play on its own - a minor reenactment of the mage's own Awakening. Non-Awakened people who go along with the mystery play gain +Gnosis/2 bonus to their rolls, while those who defy it suffer an equal amount of penalty. The mage herself qualifies as having used soft leverage when she initiates Social Maneuvering on them (whether they're trying to resist the Nimbus or not). This still rides along the mage's sympathetic connections - at Falling Wisdom, just being the owner of the diner the mage frequently eats at will throw your life into shenanigans.</li> <li><b>Signature Nimbus</b>: Spend 1 Mana reflexively to imprint High Speech, representing the Nimbus. Imprinted people, people holding an imprinted object, or people inside an imprinted area count as being under the Fractal Nimbus regardless of sympathy. Such subjects become available for use as Symbolic-level sympathetic Yantras to target the mage. The benefit the mage gets is that he can use subjects he Signed as persona Yantras worth +1 when casting spells that specifically affect them. The act of Signing the Nimbus triggers Peripheral Mage Sight, but its presence does not. It can still be viewed and studied in Active and Focused Mage Sight.</li> <li><b>Mandala Nimbus</b>: The 'aura' power. Visible under any type of Active Mage Sight when the mage is casting a spell, which can be studied further with Focused Mage Sight, but this doesn't cause any Conditions. The mage must consciously flare the Mandala by spending 1 Mana to impose the Condition. The flare triggers Peripheral Mage Sight, and is fully visible even to non-Awakened. The mage rolls Gnosis + a Resistance Attribute, chosen when designing the Condition. The Condition always bestows one positive effect and one negative effect. The positive effect gives a bonus of Gnosis/2 to an Attribute or a Skill, and the negative effect gives the same amount of penalty to another Attribute or Skill. The time required for the Condition to elapse has an inverse relation with the mage's Wisdom. Sleepers are always affected by the Condition, without resistance. Sleepwalkers contest the mage's roll with Resolve + Composure. Mages and other supernaturals who counter with their own auras enter a Clash of Wills, rolling their own dice pools.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T20:56:02-08:00","id":1018322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1016465#post1016465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- every time a spell was cast, the effects of the nimbus would trigger<br /> - if more than one mage was present, it would become a bonus/penalty-chaos<br /> - dependent on potency, it had a chance of affecting all allies with a negative effect (and a positive)<br /> - also dependent on potency, it could also grant enemies a bonus (and a penalty)</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that, unless you're doing the once-per-scene deliberate flare, it'll only affect other Mages, who currently have Active Mage Sight up, and who also have Resolve lower than the Potency of the spell. Many basic spells are Potency 1, and as such don't affect anybody (unless via some sort of weird effect you currently have Resolve 0). Many Mages have high Resolve besides. And when you ARE deliberately Flaring, the Tilt only actually hits someone with lower Resolve than successes the Mage rolls on a dicepool of their Gnosis, which for Gnosis 1-3 characters will typically not affect anybody (since, again, everyone has Resolve of at least 1).<br /> <br /> The Nimbus Tilt, in my experience, only actually comes up with high-Potency spells. I don't find it particularly difficult to remember my PCs' Resolve scores when running, and in the game I play in my PC has Resolve 4, so I only have to bother with Nimbus Tilts if the spell in question is at least Potency 5. This happens less often than you'd expect.<br /> <br /> When I looked at the &quot;every time the Mage casts a spell&quot; part initially I thought it'd be more of a headache than it was worth, but so far in-play it hasn't been much of an issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T02:09:37-08:00","id":1018383,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1909\" data-vbnamecard=\"1909\">Juhn</a> <br /> \u200bAs per the book, p. 89<br /> &quot;While characters without Mage Sight cannot see the aura, the subtle cues still affect them with the Tilt. This is almost always imperceptible, but some particularly clued-in witnesses may note when something\u2019s awry.&quot;<br /> <br /> So both the subtle nimbus and the flared one affects everybody (unless they have a higher Resolve as you mentioned). And as you said, many basic spells don't have a higher potency than 1. But attack spells also usually have a high potency, or spells that is trying to transform or alter the target will need a higher potency.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem I am having really (and my players), is that they have that extra level of &quot;be careful with casting spells&quot;. They could be boosting enemies as well as punishing allies by casting a spell.<br /> <br /> I guess I could remove it and say only Mage Sight are affected by the subtle nimbus, but then the subtle nimbus wouldn't be doing a whole lot and just be the same as the flared nimbus.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> <br /> The fractal nimbus sounds rather complex with a whole mystery play being enacted (or not). The signature nimbus trick sounds neat though, with imprinting. It is weird though, that you have to mention that the Mandala nimbus is visible under any mage sight, when even none-mage sight'ers (??) kan see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T09:19:40-08:00","id":1018482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1018383#post1018383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;While characters without Mage Sight cannot see the aura, the subtle cues still affect them with the Tilt. This is almost always imperceptible, but some particularly clued-in witnesses may note when something\u2019s awry.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This comes immediately after a sentence that calls the &quot;Interactions with other auras&quot; section which specifies that gaining a higher net quantity of successes in contesting another supernatural being's aura effect causes them to suffer your Nimbus Tilt and counts as flaring your Immediate Nimbus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T13:03:16-08:00","id":1018556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1018383#post1018383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem I am having really (and my players), is that they have that extra level of &quot;be careful with casting spells&quot;. They could be boosting enemies as well as punishing allies by casting a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>To solve this, I'd try to bring the Nimbus Tilt in line with the spell-casting rules. For example, a mage might spend a reach (or a point of Mana) to apply their tilt to all the subjects of a spell (withstood by Resolve) for the duration of the spell. Much in the same way direct attack spells allow additional reach to apply tilts, but could be used on any spell the character casts.<br /> <br /> To balance the increased cost of applying the tilt, I'd probably drop the strength being based off of Gnosis and instead offer a 1 to 5 dot merit with each dot allowing a one die bonus or penalty (or representing relative power if the tilt isn't based on adding/removing dice). Mage characters would start with at least one dot of the merit.<br /> <br /> If you want to further encourage players to use Nimbus I'd allow the immediate Nimbus to be used as a Yantra. The mage spends a Yantra slot and the player describes how the character's signature Nimbus manifests itself while the spell is cast to gain +1 die bonus on a thematically appropriate spell. They could also &quot;flare&quot; the nimbus, adding +1 Paradox die for +2 dice and the nimbus is visible to everyone present.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5098-10201","name":"10201","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T17:57:21-08:00","id":1018628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1018482#post1018482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This comes immediately after a sentence that calls the &quot;Interactions with other auras&quot; section which specifies that gaining a higher net quantity of successes in contesting another supernatural being's aura effect causes them to suffer your Nimbus Tilt and counts as flaring your Immediate Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having just looked up the passage, I agree with Satchel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages can pit their own Nimbus against the aura as per the \u201cInteractions with Other Auras\u201d rules, below. While characters without Mage Sight cannot see the aura, the subtle cues still affect them with the Tilt. This is almost always imperceptible, but some particularly clued-in witnesses may note when something\u2019s awry. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;them&quot; being affected with the Tilt is pretty clearly intended to be the other supernatural whose aura you're pitting your Nimbus against, just like how a Vampire can Lash Out with their Predatory Aura even against other supernaturals and impose the Bestial/Wanton/Competitive Condition on them, even if they don't have their own Beast to engage in the standard Vampire Predatory Aura dominance-contest (and how Werewolves can do the same thing with their Hunter's Aspects). It's basically saying &quot;If your Nimbus gets into a clash with a Predatory Aura or Hunter's Aspect, and you win the roll, you inflict the Tilt on them even if they can't actually perceive your Nimbus proper&quot;. It even points out that it clarifies what it means using the &quot;Interactions with Other Auras&quot; paragraph on the next page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interactions with other auras Other supernatural creatures tend to have aura effects that force Conditions. Sometimes this is a defense mechanism; sometimes this is a way to assert dominance. However, mages are particularly resistant to this effect. When such an effect targets your character, roll a dice pool comprised of a Resistance Attribute + Gnosis. The Resistance Attribute depends on the monster\u2019s dice pool: If it uses Strength, roll Stamina; if Presence, roll Composure; and if Intelligence, roll Resolve. This resistance is automatic, but it does count as flaring your character\u2019s Immediate Nimbus. This comes with all effects, both positive and negative. The roll acts as a contested action against whatever the other character throws at yours. Your successes subtract from his; if you net any successes beyond his, he suffers your Nimbus Tilt </div> </div> </div>The &quot;While [they] cannot see the subtle cues still affect them with the Tilt&quot; is just an attempt to justify in a fluff sense how this mechanic gets applied. The crunch text says that if you get more successes, they get whammied with your Nimbus Tilt, and that bit up there is just an attempt to explain how this can happen even if the creature isn't supposed to be able to perceive a Nimbus flare you didn't spend Mana to do deliberately in a way that's visible to all witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 12-17-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T18:19:04-08:00","id":1018633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1018383#post1018383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1909\" data-vbnamecard=\"1909\">Juhn</a><br /> \u200b<br /> The fractal nimbus sounds rather complex with a whole mystery play being enacted (or not). The signature nimbus trick sounds neat though, with imprinting. It is weird though, that you have to mention that the Mandala nimbus is visible under any mage sight, when even none-mage sight'ers (??) kan see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the mini mystery play thing was just a half-formed idea. On the other hand, the flaring I made specifically visible to everybody as a way of solving that &quot;how do they get affected by the Nimbus when they can't even see it&quot; issue. It also gives a way for mages to do quick shows of magic without actually casting spells. Attainments do that as well, but they felt more like specialized tools than a general display-of-power thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T03:25:23-08:00","id":1020817,"title":"","content":"Sounds like people agree on that it is the environment that is affect by the nimbus and not the mage himself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>10201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1018556#post1018556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To solve this, I'd try to bring the Nimbus Tilt in line with the spell-casting rules. For example, a mage might spend a reach (or a point of Mana) to apply their tilt to all the subjects of a spell (withstood by Resolve) for the duration of the spell. Much in the same way direct attack spells allow additional reach to apply tilts, but could be used on any spell the character casts.<br /> <br /> To balance the increased cost of applying the tilt, I'd probably drop the strength being based off of Gnosis and instead offer a 1 to 5 dot merit with each dot allowing a one die bonus or penalty (or representing relative power if the tilt isn't based on adding/removing dice). Mage characters would start with at least one dot of the merit.<br /> <br /> If you want to further encourage players to use Nimbus I'd allow the immediate Nimbus to be used as a Yantra. The mage spends a Yantra slot and the player describes how the character's signature Nimbus manifests itself while the spell is cast to gain +1 die bonus on a thematically appropriate spell. They could also &quot;flare&quot; the nimbus, adding +1 Paradox die for +2 dice and the nimbus is visible to everyone present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really like the using the nimbus-as-a-yantra-idea. Might have possibilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016039-does-the-nimbus-affect-the-owner?p=1018633#post1018633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the mini mystery play thing was just a half-formed idea. On the other hand, the flaring I made specifically visible to everybody as a way of solving that &quot;how do they get affected by the Nimbus when they can't even see it&quot; issue. It also gives a way for mages to do quick shows of magic without actually casting spells. Attainments do that as well, but they felt more like specialized tools than a general display-of-power thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe there is no reason to have a suttle Nimbus with a mechanical effect. It already does some things like reveal you as a mage and is imprintet on the spells you cast (or so I believe it is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}